unit("Cardiac Action Potentials and Vaughan Williams Classification",
     "Part 1 starts from the action potential: myocardial cells contract and eject blood after an action potential, while the SA node spontaneously depolarizes to generate heart rate. Myocardial depolarization is Na+-driven, the plateau uses K+, Ca2+ and inward Na+ channels, and repolarization uses delayed-rectifier K+. The first antiarrhythmic map is Vaughan Williams: class I targets Na+ channels, class II β receptors, class III K+ channels, class IV Ca2+ channels and class V miscellaneous agents.")
q(69, "A myocardial cell action potential produces:", ["Contraction and ejection of blood", "Only renin release", "Only bronchodilation", "Only aqueous humour reduction"], "The myocardial-cell label says contraction → ejection of blood on receiving action potential.")
q(69, "The peak inward Na+ channel opens during which myocardial action-potential event?", ["Depolarization", "Repolarization", "Hyperpolarization only", "Digitalization"], "Under depolarization, the first line says peak inward Na+ channel opens.")
q(69, "During the myocardial plateau phase, the early rectifier channel that opens is:", ["K+", "Cl-", "Mg2+", "H+"], "The plateau list begins early rectifier K+ channel: open.")
q(69, "The plateau phase also includes opening of:", ["Ca2+ channels", "Only Na+-K+ ATPase", "Renin channels", "PDE5 channels"], "The plateau list includes Ca2+ channel: open.")
q(69, "Early and late inward channels in the plateau phase carry:", ["Na+", "K+ only", "Chloride only", "Iodide only"], "The plateau list states early inward Na+ and late inward Na+ channels open.")
q(69, "Myocardial repolarization is produced by opening of:", ["Delayed rectifier K+ channels", "Peak inward Na+ channels", "Funny channels only", "Adenosine receptors"], "The repolarization line says delayed rectifier K+ channel opening.")
q(69, "The SA node is described as generating heart rate by:", ["Spontaneous depolarization", "Na+-K+ ATPase blockade", "Renal renin release", "Aldosterone secretion"], "The SA-node label says spontaneous depolarization generates heart rate.")
q(69, "Initiation of SA nodal depolarization is through funny channels carrying:", ["Na+/K+", "Only Ca2+", "Only Cl-", "Only iodide"], "The SA-node list says funny channels (Na+/K+) generate If.")
q(69, "The current generated by funny channels is called:", ["If, the funny current", "IKr, the delayed current", "INa late current", "ICa toxic current"], "The page labels it generate If (funny current).")
q(69, "In the SA node, depolarization plus plateau phase uses opening of:", ["Ca2+ channels", "α1 receptors", "AChE channels", "Neprilysin"], "The SA-node list says depolarization + plateau phase: Ca2+ channels open.")
q(69, "SA nodal repolarization plus hyperpolarization is produced by opening of:", ["K+ channels", "Ca2+ channels only", "Funny channels only", "β1 receptors"], "The SA-node list says repolarization + hyperpolarization: K+ channel open.")
q(69, "Vaughan Williams class I antiarrhythmics are:", ["Na+ channel blockers", "β blockers", "K+ channel blockers", "Ca2+ channel blockers"], "The classification lists class I as Na+ channel blockers.")
q(69, "Vaughan Williams class II antiarrhythmics are:", ["β blockers", "Na+ channel blockers", "K+ channel blockers", "Direct renin inhibitors"], "Class II is listed as β blockers.")
q(69, "Vaughan Williams class III antiarrhythmics are:", ["K+ channel blockers", "β blockers", "Ca2+ channel blockers", "Adenosine only"], "Class III is listed as K+ channel blockers.")
q(70, "Vaughan Williams class IV antiarrhythmics are:", ["Ca2+ channel blockers", "Na+ channel blockers", "β blockers", "Nitrates"], "At the top of page 70, class IV is Ca2+ channel blockers.")
q(70, "Class V miscellaneous antiarrhythmics on the page include:", ["Adenosine, MgSO4, atropine and digoxin", "Prazosin, terazosin, doxazosin and silodosin", "Hydralazine, minoxidil, diazoxide and fenoldopam", "Captopril, lisinopril, losartan and aliskiren"], "Class V is listed as miscellaneous with adenosine, MgSO4, atropine and digoxin.")

unit("SVT/PSVT Pathology and AV Nodal Treatment Preference",
     "SVT/PSVT is explained as a fast atrial rhythm driving AV nodal action, increasing ventricular rate and risking incomplete ventricular contraction, ventricular fibrillation and arrest. The treatment aim is to block the AV node. Adenosine is the IV DOC for acute management, β blockers such as esmolol/metoprolol are limited by bronchoconstriction, diltiazem/verapamil cover acute and long-term management, and oral digoxin is for long-term management.")
q(70, "SVT/PSVT in the chapter is categorized under:", ["Atrial arrhythmias", "Ventricular arrhythmias only", "CHF inotropes", "Renin system inhibitors"], "The heading says atrial arrhythmias before SVT/PSVT.")
q(70, "The abbreviation PSVT stands for:", ["Paroxysmal supraventricular tachycardia", "Persistent sinus ventricular tachycardia", "Pulmonary systemic venous tachycardia", "Post-synaptic vagal tachycardia"], "The page writes Supra Ventricular Tachycardia/Paroxysmal Supraventricular Tachycardia.")
q(70, "In SVT/PSVT, increased atrial contraction rate acts through the:", ["AV node", "Renal JG cell", "Na+-K+ ATPase", "Prostatic urethra"], "The pathology flow shows ↑ rate of atrial contraction → AV nodal action.")
