q(72, "In ischemia, increased Ca2+ permeability causes:", ["Persistent depolarization by Ca2+", "Immediate hyperpolarization by K+", "Renin release", "Aqueous humour excess"], "The flow says persistent depolarisation of cell by Ca2+.")
q(72, "The Na+ channel state targeted by lidocaine in ischemic cells is:", ["Closed state", "Open state only", "Absent state", "Ligand-gated state"], "The diagram labels Na+ channel closed state beside lidocaine/amiodarone treatment.")
