q(73, "Digoxin creates a large ventricular action potential by increasing intracellular:", ["Ca2+", "K+ only", "Iodide", "cGMP"], "The flow says digoxin → ↑ intracellular Ca2+ in ventricular cell → large AP.")
q(73, "A large ventricular action potential leaves closed Na+ channels available for:", ["Longer duration", "Shorter duration", "No duration", "Only renal filtration"], "The digoxin flow says closed Na+ channels available for longer duration.")
q(73, "Lidocaine is administered IV because it has:", ["High first-pass metabolism", "No first-pass metabolism", "Only topical absorption", "Poor renal excretion only"], "The route line says IV (high first-pass metabolism).")
q(73, "Lidocaine is contraindicated in atrial arrhythmias because atrial cells have:", ["Small action potentials with short closed-Na+ channel duration", "Large action potentials with long closed-Na+ channel duration", "No Na+ channels", "Only funny channels"], "The C/I flow says atrial cell → small AP → closed Na+ channels available for short duration → ineffective.")
q(73, "The earliest sign of lidocaine toxicity is:", ["Nystagmus", "Pulmonary fibrosis", "Xanthopsia", "Alopecia"], "The side-effect list states nystagmus: earliest sign of toxicity.")
q(73, "Another neurologic side effect of lidocaine is:", ["Paresthesia", "Floppy iris", "Hirsutism", "Dry cough"], "Paresthesia is listed under side effects.")
q(73, "If lidocaine causes seizures, which Na+ channel blocker is contraindicated for treatment?", ["Phenytoin", "Mexiletine", "Flecainide", "Adenosine"], "The seizure note says phenytoin (Na+ channel blocker) is C/I for Rx.")
q(73, "Mexiletine is a derivative of:", ["Lidocaine", "Quinidine", "Adenosine", "Digoxin"], "The mexiletine line says derivative of lidocaine.")
