q(74, "Amiodarone has a lower torsades risk because of its:", ["Ca2+ channel-blocking action", "Direct renin inhibition", "Aldehyde dehydrogenase activation", "β3 agonism"], "The Ca2+ channel blocker line is followed by ↓ risk of torsades.")
q(74, "Ibutilide is the:", ["Shortest-acting K+ channel blocker", "Longest-acting antiarrhythmic", "Only oral nitrate", "DOC for BPH"], "The ibutilide note says shortest acting K+ channel blocker.")
