q(75, "Amiodarone can cause hypotension through:", ["α1 block", "α2 agonism", "β3 agonism", "Direct renin inhibition"], "Side effect number 6 says alpha-1 block: hypotension.")
q(75, "The most common pigmentation with amiodarone is:", ["Brown skin pigmentation", "Yellow vision", "Floppy iris", "Retinal detachment"], "The skin line says brown pigmentation (m/c pigmentation).")
q(75, "Amiodarone photosensitivity is managed with:", ["Full skin coverage plus sunscreen", "Stopping all water intake", "Defibrillation", "PDE5 blockers"], "The skin side-effect note says Rx: full skin coverage + sunscreen.")
q(75, "Amiodarone thyroid toxicity is more often:", ["Hypothyroidism in plain dwellers", "Hyperthyroidism in plain dwellers", "No thyroid effect", "Only thyroid cancer"], "The thyroid line says hypothyroid (plain dwellers) > hyperthyroid (hilly areas).")
q(75, "Which toxicity is specifically noted as absent with amiodarone?", ["Nephrotoxicity", "Pulmonary fibrosis", "Corneal deposits", "Photosensitivity"], "The note says no nephrotoxicity seen.")
q(75, "Dronedarone is a derivative of amiodarone without:", ["Iodine", "Na+ channel blockade", "Any antiarrhythmic use", "Carbon atoms"], "The dronedarone line says derivative of amiodarone without iodine.")
q(75, "Compared with amiodarone, dronedarone has:", ["Less toxicity and less efficacy", "More toxicity and more efficacy", "No α/β block", "Only renal toxicity"], "The dronedarone bullets say less toxicity and less efficacy.")
q(75, "Dronedarone has more:", ["α and β block", "Nephrotoxicity", "Iodine content", "PDE5 inhibition"], "The dronedarone section says more α + β block.")

unit("Adenosine: MOA, Route, Dosing and Uses",
     "Adenosine acts on adenosine receptors to block the AV node through Gi, cause bronchoconstriction through Gq and vasodilate through Gs. Because it is rapidly taken up into cells and degraded orally by gastric acid, it must be given as an IV rapid push—6 mg, then 12 mg if there is no response. It is DOC for acute SVT/PSVT after vagal/carotid massage and can maintain controlled hypotension during surgery.")
q(76, "Adenosine blocks the AV node through which G protein?", ["Gi", "Gq", "Gs", "G12"], "The MOA list says block AV node (Gi).")
