start(21)
unit("Acute CHF Pathophysiology and IV Management",
     "Acute CHF is most commonly caused by myocardial infarction. Acute myocardial injury decreases contraction, causes blood stasis in the heart, raises back pressure into the lungs, engorges pulmonary capillaries and extravasates plasma into parenchyma, producing pulmonary edema. Clinically the patient has chest pain and breathlessness; IV treatment of choice is dobutamine plus furosemide.")
q(77, "The most common cause of acute CHF in the chapter is:", ["Myocardial infarction", "Rheumatic heart disease", "Cardiomyopathy only", "Renovascular hypertension"], "Under acute CHF, the m/c cause is myocardial infarction.")
q(77, "In acute CHF, myocardial infarction causes acute injury with decreased:", ["Contraction", "Back pressure", "Pulmonary capillary pressure only", "Aqueous humour"], "The pathophysiology diagram says acute injury (MI): ↓ contraction.")
q(77, "Reduced cardiac contraction in acute CHF causes stasis of:", ["Blood", "Bile", "Urine", "Aqueous humour"], "The heart diagram labels stasis of blood.")
q(77, "Stasis of blood in acute CHF increases back pressure toward the:", ["Lung", "Kidney only", "Prostate", "Iris"], "The diagram shows ↑ back pressure from heart to lung.")
q(77, "In the lung, acute CHF causes engorgement of:", ["Pulmonary capillaries", "Renal tubules", "Corneal vessels", "Prostatic urethra"], "The lung triangle says engorged pulmonary capillaries.")
q(77, "Engorged pulmonary capillaries lead to extravasation of plasma into:", ["Lung parenchyma", "Renal cortex", "Atrial accessory pathway", "Prostatic urethra"], "The diagram says extravasation of plasma into parenchyma.")
q(77, "The lung result of acute CHF pathophysiology is:", ["Pulmonary edema", "Pulmonary fibrosis from iodine", "Bronchial asthma", "Pneumothorax"], "The final label is pulmonary edema.")
q(77, "A clinical presentation of acute CHF is:", ["Chest pain", "Xanthopsia only", "Floppy iris", "Hirsutism"], "The clinical presentation list includes chest pain.")
q(77, "Breathlessness in acute CHF is due to:", ["Pulmonary edema", "Bronchial asthma always", "Renal failure only", "Atrial flutter only"], "The clinical list says breathlessness: due to pulmonary edema.")
q(77, "The route of drug administration in acute CHF management is:", ["IV", "Oral only", "Topical", "Inhaled only"], "The management section says route of administration: IV.")
q(77, "The treatment of choice for acute CHF is:", ["Dobutamine plus furosemide", "Sacubitril plus valsartan only", "Digoxin plus atropine", "Sildenafil plus tadalafil"], "The acute CHF management line says TOC: dobutamine + furosemide.")

unit("Acute CHF Inotropes and Pulmonary Edema Drugs",
     "Acute CHF management combines drugs that increase contraction and drugs that quickly relieve pulmonary edema. Dobutamine stimulates β1-Gs to raise cAMP and contractility without affecting heart rate; PDE3 inhibitors raise cAMP as inodilators; levosimendan opens K+ channels and sensitizes myocardium to Ca2+. Furosemide venodilates via prostaglandins and diureses; if there is no response, nitroglycerin and then nesiritide can be considered.")
q(77, "Dobutamine increases contraction by stimulating:", ["β1 receptors of the Gs subtype", "β3 receptors in bladder", "α1a receptors in prostate", "Adenosine Gi receptors"], "The dobutamine MOA says stimulate β1 receptor (Gs subtype).")
q(77, "β1-Gs stimulation by dobutamine increases:", ["cAMP", "cGMP only", "Uric acid", "Aldosterone only"], "The dobutamine flow says ↑ cAMP → ↑ cardiac contraction.")
